<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ma'mun ibn Muhammad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/997">997</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Ma'mun I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ma'mun ibn Muhammad was the emir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gurganj">Gurganj</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazm">Khwarazm</a> who founded the Ma'munid dynasty. In 995 he overthrew and killed the last Afrighid shah of Kath, uniting Khwarazm and taking the title <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazmshah">Khwarazmshah</a>. He died in 997 and was succeeded by his sons Ali and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abul-abbas-mamun">Ma'mun II</a>.</p></div>
